45 780 Td
(   - Since m * c is the linear momentum p of the photon: p = h / lambda => lambda = h / p.) Tj
T*
(   - De Broglie boldly generalized this relation to any material particle of mass m moving with) Tj
T*
(   non-relativistic velocity v:) Tj
T*
(   p = m * v => lambda = h / \(m * v\) \(de Broglie Wavelength\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Matter Wavelength in Terms of Kinetic Energy E_k:) Tj
T*
(   - Kinetic energy: E_k = 0.5 * m * v^2 = p^2 / \(2 * m\) => p = sqrt\( 2 * m * E_k \).) Tj
T*
(   - Therefore: lambda = h / sqrt\( 2 * m * E_k \).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Electron Accelerated Through Potential Difference V:) Tj
T*
(   - When an electron \(charge e = 1.602 x 10^-19 C, mass m_e = 9.109 x 10^-31 kg\) is accelerated) Tj
T*
(   from rest across potential difference V, the work done equals kinetic energy: E_k = e * V.) Tj
T*
(   - Substituting into the wavelength formula:) Tj
T*
(   lambda = h / sqrt\( 2 * m_e * e * V \).) Tj
T*
(   - Substituting physical constants:) Tj
T*
(   h = 6.626 x 10^-34 J*s, m_e = 9.109 x 10^-31 kg, e = 1.602 x 10^-19 C.) Tj
T*
(   lambda = \(6.626 x 10^-34\) / sqrt\( 2 * 9.109 x 10^-31 * 1.602 x 10^-19 * V \)) Tj
T*
(   = \(6.626 x 10^-34\) / [ 5.402 x 10^-25 * sqrt\(V\) ] = \(1.2265 x 10^-9\) / sqrt\(V\) meters.) Tj
T*
(   lambda = 1.227 / sqrt\(V\) nm = 12.27 / sqrt\(V\) Angstroms.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
