/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 3:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the Davisson-Germer experiment and explain how it provided the first conclusive experimental proof of de Broglie's matter wave hypothesis.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Experimental Apparatus Setup:) Tj
T*
(   - An electron gun consisting of a heated tungsten filament emits electrons, which are) Tj
T*
(   accelerated through a variable high-voltage anode V \(typically 40 to 68 Volts\).) Tj
T*
(   - A fine collimator directs a narrow, parallel beam of monoenergetic electrons onto the target.) Tj
T*
(   - The target is a single crystal of Nickel \(Ni\) cut along a specific crystallographic plane.) Tj
T*
(   - An electrostatic Faraday cylinder collector is mounted on a graduated circular scale that can) Tj
T*
(   rotate between 20 and 90 degrees to measure scattered electron current I as a function of) Tj
T*
(   scattering angle phi.) Tj
T*
(   - The entire apparatus is enclosed in an ultra-high vacuum chamber.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Experimental Observations:) Tj
T*
(   - When the accelerating voltage was set to V = 54 Volts, a prominent, sharp peak in the) Tj
T*
(   scattered electron intensity appeared at scattering angle phi = 50 degrees.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Analysis using de Broglie's Hypothesis:) Tj
T*
(   - According to de Broglie's formula, the theoretical wavelength of 54 eV electrons is:) Tj
T*
(   lambda_deBroglie = 1.227 / sqrt\(54\) = 1.227 / 7.348 = 0.167 nm \(1.67 Angstroms\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Analysis using Bragg's X-Ray Diffraction Law:) Tj
T*
(   - From X-ray crystallography, nickel has a face-centered cubic lattice with interplanar spacing) Tj
T*
(   d = 0.091 nm \(0.91 Angstroms\).) Tj
T*
(   - The glancing angle theta with the atomic planes is related to scattering angle phi by:) Tj
T*
(   theta = 90 deg - \(phi / 2\) = 90 deg - 25 deg = 65 degrees.) Tj
T*
(   - Applying Bragg's law for first-order constructive interference \(n = 1\):) Tj
T*
(   lambda_Bragg = 2 * d * sin\(theta\) = 2 * \(0.091 nm\) * sin\(65 deg\) = 0.182 * 0.9063 = 0.165 nm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Conclusive Proof:) Tj
T*
(   - The experimentally measured Bragg diffraction wavelength \(0.165 nm\) matched de Broglie's) Tj
T*
(   theoretical prediction \(0.167 nm\) within 1.2% experimental accuracy.) Tj
T*
ET

