(>> Solution to Question 7:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the 1D Time-Independent Schrodinger Equation \(TISE\) from the Time-Dependent Schrodinger Equation \(TDSE\) using the method of separation of variables.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The 1D Time-Dependent Schrodinger Equation \(TDSE\):) Tj
T*
(   - For a particle of mass m moving in a time-independent potential V\(x\):) Tj
T*
(   i * hbar * \(dPsi\(x,t\) / dt\) = - \(hbar^2 / \(2 * m\)\) * \(d^2Psi\(x,t\) / dx^2\) + V\(x\) * Psi\(x,t\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Separation of Variables:) Tj
T*
(   - Assume the total wave function can be factored into a product of a purely spatial function) Tj
T*
(   psi\(x\) and a purely temporal function phi\(t\):) Tj
T*
(   Psi\(x,t\) = psi\(x\) * phi\(t\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Substitution into TDSE:) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute into the differential equation:) Tj
T*
(   i * hbar * psi\(x\) * \(dphi\(t\) / dt\) = - \(hbar^2 / \(2*m\)\) * phi\(t\) * \(d^2psi\(x\) / dx^2\) + V\(x\) *) Tj
T*
(   psi\(x\) * phi\(t\).) Tj
T*
(   - Divide both sides by the product psi\(x\) * phi\(t\):) Tj
T*
(   i * hbar * \(1 / phi\(t\)\) * \(dphi\(t\) / dt\) = - \(hbar^2 / \(2*m\)\) * \(1 / psi\(x\)\) * \(d^2psi\(x\) /) Tj
T*
(   dx^2\) + V\(x\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Separation Constant E:) Tj
T*
(   - The left-hand side is a function strictly of time t alone, while the right-hand side is a) Tj
T*
(   function strictly of space x alone.) Tj
T*
(   - For this equality to hold for all arbitrary x and t, both sides must equal a common) Tj
T*
(   separation constant, which has the physical dimension of Total Energy E.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Temporal Equation and Solution:) Tj
T*
(   - i * hbar * \(1 / phi\) * \(dphi / dt\) = E => dphi / dt = - \(i * E / hbar\) * phi.) Tj
T*
(   - Integrating yields: phi\(t\) = exp\( - i * E * t / hbar \).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   6. Spatial Equation \(Time-Independent Schrodinger Equation\):) Tj
T*
(   - - \(hbar^2 / \(2*m\)\) * \(d^2psi / dx^2\) + V\(x\) * psi = E * psi.) Tj
T*
(   - Rearranging into standard form:) Tj
T*
(   d^2psi / dx^2 + \(2 * m / hbar^2\) * [ E - V\(x\) ] * psi\(x\) = 0 \(TISE\). \(Q.E.D.\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 8:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Solve the 1D Time-Independent Schrodinger Equation for a particle of mass m confined in an infinitely deep potential well of width L \(0 <= x <= L\). Obtain the normalized wave functions and quantized energy eigenvalues.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Potential Function Definition:) Tj
T*
(   - V\(x\) = 0 for 0 < x < L \(inside the well\).) Tj
T*
(   - V\(x\) = infinity for x <= 0 and x >= L \(outside the well\).) Tj
T*
(   - Since V = infinity outside, the particle cannot exist outside: psi\(x\) = 0 for x <= 0 and x >=) Tj
T*
(   L.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. TISE Inside the Well \(V = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   - d^2psi / dx^2 + \(2*m*E / hbar^2\) * psi = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Define wavevector k^2 = \(2*m*E / hbar^2\):) Tj
T*
(   d^2psi / dx^2 + k^2 * psi = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - General harmonic solution: psi\(x\) = A * sin\(k*x\) + B * cos\(k*x\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Applying Boundary Conditions:) Tj
T*
(   - Boundary condition 1 at x = 0: psi\(0\) = 0.) Tj
T*
ET

