(   [Problem Statement]: An electron is trapped in an infinitely deep 1D potential well of width L = 0.20 nm. Calculate: \(a\) energy of the first three quantum levels in eV, \(b\) frequency and wavelength of the photon emitted during transition from n = 3 to n = 1, \(c\) probability of finding the electron between x = 0 and x = 0.05 nm in the ground state.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Given Data:) Tj
T*
(   - Well width L = 0.20 nm = 2.0 x 10^-10 m.) Tj
T*
(   - Electron mass m_e = 9.109 x 10^-31 kg; Planck constant h = 6.626 x 10^-34 J*s.) Tj
T*
(   - 1 eV = 1.602 x 10^-19 Joules.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. \(a\) Energy of First Three Quantum Levels:) Tj
T*
(   - Ground state \(n = 1\): E1 = h^2 / \(8 * m_e * L^2\)) Tj
T*
(   E1 = \(6.626 x 10^-34\)^2 / [ 8 * 9.109 x 10^-31 * \(2.0 x 10^-10\)^2 ]) Tj
T*
(   = \(4.390 x 10^-67\) / [ 8 * 9.109 x 10^-31 * 4.0 x 10^-20 ]) Tj
T*
(   = \(4.390 x 10^-67\) / \(2.915 x 10^-49\) = 1.506 x 10^-18 Joules.) Tj
T*
(   In eV: E1 = 1.506 x 10^-18 / \(1.602 x 10^-19\) = 9.40 eV.) Tj
T*
ET

