(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the concept of quantum operators, eigenvalues, and expectation values. Show that the momentum operator p_hat = -i*hbar*\(d/dx\) is Hermitian.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Quantum Operators and Postulates:) Tj
T*
(   - In quantum mechanics, every classical physical observable A is associated with a linear) Tj
T*
(   operator A_hat.) Tj
T*
(   - If a measurement of A is performed on a state psi, the only possible outcomes are the) Tj
T*
(   eigenvalues a_n of the eigenvalue equation:) Tj
T*
(   A_hat * psi_n = a_n * psi_n.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Expectation Value:) Tj
T*
(   - The expectation value <A> is the statistical average of measurements performed on an ensemble) Tj
T*
(   of identically prepared states:) Tj
T*
(   <A> = Integral_{-inf}^{+inf} psi*\(x\) * A_hat * psi\(x\) dx.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Hermitian Operator Condition:) Tj
T*
(   - Because physical measurements yield real numbers, all quantum operators must have real) Tj
T*
(   eigenvalues, which requires them to be Hermitian:) Tj
T*
(   Integral f* * \(A_hat * g\) dx = Integral \(A_hat * f\)* * g dx for all square-integrable functions) Tj
T*
(   f and g.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Proof that Momentum Operator p_hat = -i*hbar*\(d/dx\) is Hermitian:) Tj
T*
(   - Consider the integral: I = Integral_{-inf}^{+inf} f*\(x\) * [ -i*hbar * \(dg/dx\) ] dx = -i*hbar) Tj
T*
(   * Integral_{-inf}^{+inf} f* * \(dg/dx\) dx.) Tj
T*
(   - Integrate by parts: u = f*, dv = \(dg/dx\) dx => du = \(df*/dx\) dx, v = g:) Tj
T*
(   I = -i*hbar * [ f*\(x\)*g\(x\) |_{-inf}^{+inf} - Integral_{-inf}^{+inf} \(df*/dx\) * g dx ].) Tj
T*
(   - For square-integrable wave functions, f\(x\) and g\(x\) vanish at infinity: [ f* * g) Tj
T*
(   ]_{-inf}^{+inf} = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Therefore:) Tj
T*
(   I = + i * hbar * Integral_{-inf}^{+inf} \(df*/dx\) * g dx = Integral_{-inf}^{+inf} [ -i*hbar *) Tj
T*
(   \(df/dx\) ]* * g dx.) Tj
T*
(   I = Integral_{-inf}^{+inf} \(p_hat * f\)* * g dx. \(Q.E.D.\)) Tj
T*
(   - This proves that p_hat is strictly Hermitian and guarantees real momentum eigenvalues.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

