12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the quantum mechanical principles behind the Transmission Electron Microscope \(TEM\) and compare its structural characterization capabilities with light optical microscopy.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Diffraction Limit of Classical Optical Microscopy:) Tj
T*
(   - According to Abbe's diffraction limit, the spatial resolution delta_r of an optical) Tj
T*
(   microscope is bounded by wavelength lambda:) Tj
T*
(   delta_r = 0.61 * lambda / NA.) Tj
T*
(   - For visible light \(lambda ~ 500 nm, NA ~ 1.4\), the ultimate resolution is limited to ~ 200 nm) Tj
T*
(   \(0.2 micrometers\).) Tj
T*
(   - Sub-micron features \(cement C-S-H gel pores, steel dislocation networks\) cannot be resolved.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. De Broglie Wavelength of Relativistic Electrons:) Tj
T*
(   - In a TEM, electrons accelerated through 100 kV to 300 kV possess de Broglie wavelengths of:) Tj
T*
(   lambda = 1.227 / sqrt\(V\) nm ~= 0.0037 nm \(at 100 kV\) down to 0.0019 nm \(at 300 kV\).) Tj
T*
(   - This wavelength is ~ 100,000 times shorter than visible light!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Construction and Ray Optics:) Tj
T*
(   - High-voltage electron gun \(field emission gun FEG\) emits coherent electrons.) Tj
T*
(   - Magnetic electromagnetic coils serve as condenser, objective, and projector lenses.) Tj
T*
(   - The electron beam transmits through an ultra-thin specimen \(< 100 nm thick\).) Tj
T*
(   - Objective apertures select transmitted or Bragg-diffracted electron beams to form) Tj
T*
(   Bright-Field \(BF\) or Dark-Field \(DF\) images and Selected Area Electron Diffraction \(SAED\)) Tj
T*
(   patterns.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Civil Engineering Structural Applications:) Tj
T*
(   - Imaging the interlocking crystalline nanostructure of tobermorite and jennite sheets in) Tj
T*
(   cement gel.) Tj
T*
(   - Direct visualization of dislocation pinning and grain boundary carbide precipitates in) Tj
T*
(   high-strength seismic structural steel rebars.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
