/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Calculate the expectation values <x>, <x^2>, <p>, and <p^2> for a particle in the ground state of an infinite 1D potential well of width L, and verify Heisenberg's uncertainty principle.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Ground State Wave Function \(n = 1\):) Tj
T*
(   - psi_1\(x\) = sqrt\(2 / L\) * sin\(pi * x / L\) for 0 <= x <= L.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Expectation Values of Position:) Tj
T*
(   - <x> = Integral_0^L x * \(2/L\) * sin^2\(pi*x/L\) dx = \(2/L\) * \(L^2 / 4\) = L / 2.) Tj
T*
(   - <x^2> = Integral_0^L x^2 * \(2/L\) * sin^2\(pi*x/L\) dx = L^2 * \( 1/3 - 1 / \(2*pi^2\) \) ~= 0.2827) Tj
T*
(   * L^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Variance in position:) Tj
T*
(   \(Delta_x\)^2 = <x^2> - <x>^2 = L^2 * \( 1/3 - 1/\(2*pi^2\) \) - \(L/2\)^2 = L^2 * \( 1/12 - 1/\(2*pi^2\)) Tj
T*
(   \) = 0.03267 * L^2.) Tj
T*
(   Delta_x = 0.1807 * L.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Expectation Values of Momentum:) Tj
T*
(   - p_hat * psi = -i*hbar * \(d/dx\)[ sqrt\(2/L\)*sin\(pi*x/L\) ] =) Tj
T*
(   -i*hbar*\(pi/L\)*sqrt\(2/L\)*cos\(pi*x/L\).) Tj
T*
(   - <p> = Integral_0^L psi* * \(p_hat * psi\) dx = -i*hbar*\(pi/L\)*\(2/L\) * Integral_0^L) Tj
T*
ET

