(   [Problem Statement]: Derive Compton's formula for the wavelength shift Delta_lambda of a scattered photon using relativistic conservation of energy and linear momentum.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Relativistic Kinematics Setup:) Tj
T*
(   - Incident photon: Energy E = h*nu, momentum p = h*nu / c along x-axis.) Tj
T*
(   - Target electron initially at rest: Rest energy E_0 = m_e * c^2, momentum p_e = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Scattered photon: Energy E' = h*nu', momentum p' = h*nu' / c at angle theta with x-axis.) Tj
T*
(   - Recoil electron: Total relativistic energy E_e = sqrt\( p_e^2 * c^2 + m_e^2 * c^4 \), recoil) Tj
T*
(   momentum p_e at angle phi.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Conservation of Linear Momentum:) Tj
T*
ET

