BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: An X-ray beam of wavelength 0.071 nm is scattered by electrons in a carbon target. Calculate: \(a\) Compton wavelength of an electron, \(b\) scattered wavelength at 90 degrees, \(c\) scattered wavelength at 180 degrees \(backscattering\), \(d\) maximum kinetic energy transferred to the recoil electron.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Given Data:) Tj
T*
(   - Incident wavelength: lambda = 0.071 nm = 7.10 x 10^-11 m.) Tj
T*
(   - Electron mass m_e = 9.109 x 10^-31 kg; c = 3.0 x 10^8 m/s; h = 6.626 x 10^-34 J*s.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. \(a\) Compton Wavelength lambda_c:) Tj
T*
(   - lambda_c = h / \(m_e * c\) = \(6.626 x 10^-34\) / [ 9.109 x 10^-31 * 3.0 x 10^8 ] = 2.425 x) Tj
T*
(   10^-12 m = 0.002425 nm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. \(b\) Scattered Wavelength at theta = 90 degrees:) Tj
T*
(   - cos\(90 deg\) = 0 => 1 - cos\(90 deg\) = 1.0.) Tj
T*
(   - Delta_lambda_90 = lambda_c * \(1 - 0\) = 0.002425 nm.) Tj
T*
(   - lambda'_90 = lambda + Delta_lambda_90 = 0.0710 + 0.002425 = 0.073425 nm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. \(c\) Scattered Wavelength at theta = 180 degrees \(Backscattering\):) Tj
T*
(   - cos\(180 deg\) = -1 => 1 - cos\(180 deg\) = 2.0.) Tj
T*
(   - Delta_lambda_max = 2 * lambda_c = 2 * 0.002425 nm = 0.00485 nm.) Tj
T*
(   - lambda'_180 = lambda + Delta_lambda_max = 0.0710 + 0.00485 = 0.07585 nm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. \(d\) Maximum Kinetic Energy Transferred to Electron K_max:) Tj
T*
(   - K_max = E_incident - E'_scattered = h*c * [ 1/lambda - 1/lambda'_180 ]) Tj
T*
(   - 1/lambda = 1 / \(7.10 x 10^-11 m\) = 1.4085 x 10^10 m^-1.) Tj
T*
(   - 1/lambda' = 1 / \(7.585 x 10^-11 m\) = 1.3184 x 10^10 m^-1.) Tj
T*
(   - Difference = 1.4085x10^10 - 1.3184x10^10 = 9.01 x 10^8 m^-1.) Tj
T*
ET

