(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the concept of quantum degeneracy in a 3D cubical potential well of side L. Calculate the energies and degeneracies of the first four energy levels.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. 3D Cubical Well Wave Functions and Energies:) Tj
T*
(   - A particle of mass m confined in a 3D box \(0 <= x, y, z <= L\) has separable wave functions:) Tj
T*
(   psi_{nx,ny,nz}\(x,y,z\) = \(2/L\)^\(3/2\) * sin\(nx*pi*x / L\) * sin\(ny*pi*y / L\) * sin\(nz*pi*z / L\).) Tj
T*
(   - Total energy eigenvalues:) Tj
T*
(   E = [ pi^2 * hbar^2 / \(2 * m * L^2\) ] * \( nx^2 + ny^2 + nz^2 \) = E1 * \( nx^2 + ny^2 + nz^2 \),) Tj
T*
(   where E1 = h^2 / \(8 * m * L^2\) and nx, ny, nz = 1, 2, 3, ...) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Definition of Degeneracy:) Tj
T*
(   - Degeneracy g is the number of linearly independent wave functions \(eigenstates\) that) Tj
T*
(   correspond to the identical energy eigenvalue.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Calculation for the First Four Levels:) Tj
T*
(   - \(a\) Level 1 \(Ground State\):) Tj
T*
(   \(nx, ny, nz\) = \(1, 1, 1\). Sum of squares = 1 + 1 + 1 = 3.) Tj
T*
(   Energy: E = 3 * E1. Degeneracy g = 1 \(Non-degenerate\).) Tj
T*
(   - \(b\) Level 2:) Tj
T*
(   Permutations: \(2, 1, 1\), \(1, 2, 1\), \(1, 1, 2\). Sum of squares = 4 + 1 + 1 = 6.) Tj
T*
(   Energy: E = 6 * E1. Degeneracy g = 3 \(Three-fold degenerate\).) Tj
T*
(   - \(c\) Level 3:) Tj
T*
(   Permutations: \(2, 2, 1\), \(2, 1, 2\), \(1, 2, 2\). Sum of squares = 4 + 4 + 1 = 9.) Tj
T*
(   Energy: E = 9 * E1. Degeneracy g = 3 \(Three-fold degenerate\).) Tj
T*
(   - \(d\) Level 4:) Tj
T*
(   Permutations: \(3, 1, 1\), \(1, 3, 1\), \(1, 1, 3\). Sum of squares = 9 + 1 + 1 = 11.) Tj
T*
(   Energy: E = 11 * E1. Degeneracy g = 3 \(Three-fold degenerate\).) Tj
T*
(   - \(Note: Level \(2, 2, 2\) has sum of squares = 12, non-degenerate g = 1\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
