(   [Problem Statement]: A particle of mass m is in the first excited state \(n = 2\) of an infinite well of width L. Find: \(a\) positions where the probability density is maximum, \(b\) positions of nodes where the probability is zero, \(c\) the probability of finding the particle in the interval 0 <= x <= L/4.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. First Excited State Wave Function \(n = 2\):) Tj
T*
(   - psi_2\(x\) = sqrt\(2 / L\) * sin\( 2 * pi * x / L \) for 0 <= x <= L.) Tj
T*
(   - Probability density: P_2\(x\) = |psi_2\(x\)|^2 = \(2 / L\) * sin^2\( 2 * pi * x / L \).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. \(a\) Positions of Maximum Probability Density:) Tj
T*
(   - Maxima occur when sin^2\( 2*pi*x / L \) = 1 => 2*pi*x / L = pi/2, 3*pi/2.) Tj
T*
(   - x_max1 = L / 4) Tj
T*
(   - x_max2 = 3 * L / 4.) Tj
T*
(   - Peak probability density at both points: P_max = 2 / L.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. \(b\) Positions of Nodal Points \(Zero Probability\):) Tj
T*
(   - Nodes occur where sin\( 2*pi*x / L \) = 0 inside the well \(excluding walls x=0 and x=L\):) Tj
T*
(   2*pi*x / L = pi => x_node = L / 2 \(exact center of the well\).) Tj
T*
(   - The particle has absolute zero probability of ever being detected at x = L/2, yet it) Tj
T*
(   transitions freely between the left and right halves of the box!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. \(c\) Probability in Interval 0 <= x <= L/4:) Tj
T*
(   - P = Integral_0^{L/4} \(2/L\) * sin^2\( 2*pi*x / L \) dx) Tj
T*
(   = \(1/L\) * Integral_0^{L/4} [ 1 - cos\(4*pi*x / L\) ] dx) Tj
T*
(   = \(1/L\) * [ x - \(L / 4*pi\) * sin\(4*pi*x / L\) ]_0^{L/4}) Tj
T*
(   = \(1/L\) * [ L/4 - \(L / 4*pi\) * sin\(pi\) ] = \(1/L\) * \(L/4 - 0\) = 1/4 = 0.250 \(25.0%\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
