(   - In classical mechanics, observable multiplication is commutative \(x*p = p*x\).) Tj
T*
(   - In quantum mechanics, operators act sequentially on wave functions, and operator) Tj
T*
(   multiplication is generally non-commutative.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Proof that [x, p] = i*hbar:) Tj
T*
(   - Let f\(x\) be an arbitrary differentiable test wave function.) Tj
T*
(   - Evaluate [x_hat, p_hat] acting on f\(x\):) Tj
T*
(   [x_hat, p_hat] f\(x\) = \( x_hat * p_hat - p_hat * x_hat \) f\(x\) = x_hat * \(p_hat f\) - p_hat *) Tj
T*
(   \(x_hat f\).) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute x_hat = x and p_hat = -i*hbar * \(d/dx\):) Tj
T*
(   x_hat * \(p_hat f\) = x * [ -i*hbar * \(df/dx\) ] = -i*hbar * x * \(df/dx\).) Tj
T*
(   p_hat * \(x_hat f\) = -i*hbar * \(d/dx\) [ x * f\(x\) ] = -i*hbar * [ 1 * f\(x\) + x * \(df/dx\) ]) Tj
T*
(   = -i*hbar * f\(x\) - i*hbar * x * \(df/dx\).) Tj
T*
(   - Subtracting the two expressions:) Tj
T*
(   [x_hat, p_hat] f\(x\) = -i*hbar * x * \(df/dx\) - [ -i*hbar * f\(x\) - i*hbar * x * \(df/dx\) ]) Tj
T*
(   = + i * hbar * f\(x\).) Tj
T*
(   - Since f\(x\) is completely arbitrary, the operator identity holds:) Tj
T*
(   [x_hat, p_hat] = i * hbar * I_hat. \(Q.E.D.\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Physical Consequence:) Tj
T*
(   - A fundamental theorem of linear algebra states that two operators share a common set of) Tj
T*
(   simultaneous eigenfunctions \(simultaneous diagonalization\) if and only if they commute \([A, B]) Tj
T*
(   = 0\).) Tj
T*
(   - Because [x, p] = i*hbar != 0, position and momentum do not share common eigenstates.) Tj
T*
(   - Measuring position with precision collapses the state into a spatial Dirac delta, dispersing) Tj
T*
(   momentum uncertainty to infinity, establishing the mathematical foundation of Heisenberg's) Tj
T*
(   principle.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
