(   [Problem Statement]: A beam of electrons with kinetic energy E = 50 eV is incident upon a 1D potential step of height V_0 = 30 eV. Calculate: \(a\) wavevector k1 in region 1 \(x < 0\), \(b\) wavevector k2 in region 2 \(x > 0\), \(c\) reflection coefficient R, \(d\) transmission coefficient T.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Given Data:) Tj
T*
(   - Incident energy E = 50 eV = 50 * 1.602 x 10^-19 J = 8.01 x 10^-18 J.) Tj
T*
(   - Step height V_0 = 30 eV; Region 2 kinetic energy E - V_0 = 20 eV = 3.204 x 10^-18 J.) Tj
T*
(   - Electron mass m_e = 9.109 x 10^-31 kg; hbar = 1.0546 x 10^-34 J*s.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. \(a\) Wavevector k1 in Region 1 \(x < 0, V = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   - k1 = sqrt\( 2 * m_e * E \) / hbar) Tj
T*
(   - k1 = sqrt\( 2 * 9.109 x 10^-31 * 8.01 x 10^-18 \) / \(1.0546 x 10^-34\)) Tj
T*
(   = sqrt\( 1.459 x 10^-47 \) / \(1.0546 x 10^-34\) = \(3.820 x 10^-24\) / \(1.0546 x 10^-34\) = 3.622 x) Tj
T*
(   10^10 m^-1 = 36.22 nm^-1.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. \(b\) Wavevector k2 in Region 2 \(x > 0, V = V_0\):) Tj
T*
(   - k2 = sqrt\( 2 * m_e * \(E - V_0\) \) / hbar = k1 * sqrt\( \(E - V_0\) / E \) = 36.22 * sqrt\( 20 / 50) Tj
T*
(   \) = 36.22 * sqrt\( 0.40 \) = 36.22 * 0.63246 = 22.91 nm^-1.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. \(c\) Reflection Coefficient R:) Tj
T*
(   - By matching wave functions and derivatives at boundary x = 0:) Tj
T*
(   R = [ \(k1 - k2\) / \(k1 + k2\) ]^2.) Tj
T*
(   - k1 - k2 = 36.22 - 22.91 = 13.31 nm^-1.) Tj
T*
(   - k1 + k2 = 36.22 + 22.91 = 59.13 nm^-1.) Tj
T*
(   - R = \( 13.31 / 59.13 \)^2 = \( 0.2251 \)^2 = 0.0507 = 5.07%.) Tj
T*
ET

