(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the quantum mechanical concept of probability current density J\(x,t\). Derive the quantum continuity equation and prove that probability is conserved in time.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definition of Probability Current Density J\(x,t\):) Tj
T*
(   - In analogy to electric current density in electromagnetism, probability current density) Tj
T*
(   J\(x,t\) represents the net flow rate of probability per unit area across a boundary.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Derivation from the Time-Dependent Schrodinger Equation:) Tj
T*
(   - TDSE: dPsi / dt = \(i*hbar / 2m\) * \(d^2Psi / dx^2\) - \(i / hbar\) * V * Psi.) Tj
T*
(   - Complex conjugate TDSE: dPsi* / dt = - \(i*hbar / 2m\) * \(d^2Psi* / dx^2\) + \(i / hbar\) * V *) Tj
T*
(   Psi*.) Tj
T*
(   - Rate of change of probability density P = Psi* * Psi:) Tj
T*
(   dP / dt = \(dPsi* / dt\) * Psi + Psi* * \(dPsi / dt\).) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute the derivatives:) Tj
T*
(   dP / dt = [ - \(i*hbar / 2m\)*\(d^2Psi*/dx^2\) + \(i/hbar\)*V*Psi* ] * Psi + Psi* * [ \(i*hbar /) Tj
T*
(   2m\)*\(d^2Psi/dx^2\) - \(i/hbar\)*V*Psi ].) Tj
T*
(   - The potential terms cancel: \(i/hbar\)*V*Psi**Psi - \(i/hbar\)*V*Psi**Psi = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Grouping spatial terms:) Tj
T*
(   dP / dt = \(i*hbar / 2m\) * [ Psi* * \(d^2Psi/dx^2\) - \(d^2Psi*/dx^2\) * Psi ]) Tj
T*
(   = \(i*hbar / 2m\) * \(d/dx\) [ Psi* * \(dPsi/dx\) - \(dPsi*/dx\) * Psi ].) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Quantum Continuity Equation:) Tj
T*
(   - Defining Probability Current Density J\(x,t\) as:) Tj
T*
(   J\(x,t\) = \(hbar / 2*m*i\) * [ Psi* * \(dPsi/dx\) - \(dPsi*/dx\) * Psi ] = \(hbar / m\) * Imaginary[) Tj
T*
(   Psi* * \(dPsi/dx\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - The equation becomes:) Tj
T*
(   dP / dt + dJ / dx = 0 \(Quantum Continuity Equation\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Conservation of Total Probability:) Tj
T*
(   - Integrating over all space from -infinity to +infinity:) Tj
T*
(   d/dt Integral_{-inf}^{+inf} P dx = - Integral_{-inf}^{+inf} \(dJ/dx\) dx = - [ J\(+inf\) - J\(-inf\)) Tj
T*
(   ].) Tj
T*
(   - For square-integrable states, Psi and dPsi/dx vanish at +- infinity, so J\(+inf\) = J\(-inf\) =) Tj
T*
(   0.) Tj
T*
(   - Therefore: d/dt Integral |Psi|^2 dx = 0 => Total probability is rigorously conserved for all) Tj
T*
(   time.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
