(   [Problem Statement]: Explain how the principles of quantum mechanics govern the hydration and setting of Portland cement at the sub-nanometer scale, with specific reference to Calcium-Silicate-Hydrate \(C-S-H\) gel.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Nanoscale Nature of Cement Paste:) Tj
T*
(   - Portland cement concrete is the world's most consumed manufactured civil material.) Tj
T*
(   - Its binding strength, creep, and durability originate from Calcium-Silicate-Hydrate \(C-S-H\)) Tj
T*
(   gel, a quasi-amorphous, nanoporous colloidal phase formed during tricalcium silicate \(C3S\)) Tj
T*
(   hydration:) Tj
T*
(   2 Ca3SiO5 + 11 H2O -> 3 CaO * 2 SiO2 * 8 H2O \(C-S-H\) + 3 Ca\(OH\)2.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Quantum Mechanical Interactions at the Atomic Scale:) Tj
T*
(   - \(a\) Tobermorite-Jennite Sheet Stacking: Quantum Density Functional Theory \(DFT\) calculations) Tj
T*
(   show that C-S-H consists of defective silicate dreierkette chains sandwiched between calcium) Tj
T*
(   oxide sheets separated by 1.4 nm water interlayers.) Tj
T*
(   - \(b\) Quantum Cohesive Forces: Classical DLVO colloid theory fails completely to explain cement) Tj
T*
(   cohesion because like-charged C-S-H particles carry negative surface charges in alkaline pore) Tj
T*
(   solution \(pH > 12.5\).) Tj
T*
(   * Ab-initio quantum chemical calculations reveal that divalent calcium ions \(Ca2+\) undergo) Tj
T*
(   localized quantum electrostatic correlations, forming strong ion-correlation attraction) Tj
T*
(   \(bridging bonds\) that hold cement nanoparticles together.) Tj
T*
(   - \(c\) Water Molecule Hydrogen Bonding: Confined water molecules in the 1.4 nm interlayer) Tj
T*
(   undergo quantum tunneling and hindered rotation, governing long-term concrete drying shrinkage) Tj
T*
(   and viscoelastic creep.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Civil Engineering Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   - Modern molecular engineering of ultra-high-performance concrete \(UHPC\) and low-carbon cement) Tj
T*
(   relies on quantum mechanics to optimize chemical admixtures \(graphene oxide, nanosilica\) that) Tj
T*
(   anchor directly to C-S-H silicate chains.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
